  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Colin Huang Zheng (Chinese: 黄峥; pinyin: Huáng Zhēng; born 1 January 1980) is a Chinese businessman, investor, and philanthropist. He is the founder and former CEO of the e-commerce company Pinduoduo, which is now the largest agriculture platform in China. Huang is also the owner of at least three other limited liability Cayman companies, including Pinduoduo.\nAccording to Forbes, Huang has an estimated net worth of US$27.6 billion as of 2026.",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
